/**
 * @defgroup DspCore_Examples Examples and tutorials
 * @brief Runnable, reproducible walkthroughs of the public DspCore API.
 *
 * An example is a small program intended to be read, changed and run. It
 * demonstrates a workflow and gives a human-readable result; it is therefore
 * different from a test. Tests assert contracts automatically and may exercise
 * edge cases that are deliberately not part of a first explanation. Examples
 * are closer to a MATLAB live script: source, command, output and the meaning
 * of that output live together.
 *
 * Each tutorial below contains its goal, the specific API behavior it makes
 * visible, a desktop command, representative output captured from the current
 * build, and the portable `Shared.cpp` implementation used by both the desktop
 * adapter and Arduino sketch. Filter tutorials also contain their generated
 * figure and native CSV-producing adapter.
 *
 * @section DspCore_Examples_Start Run an example
 *
 * @code{.bash}
 * ./scripts/build.sh macos_arm64 --examples-on
 * ./build/macos_arm64/bin/Debug/DspCore_Core_Version_d
 * @endcode
 *
 * The source layout intentionally keeps the tutorial logic portable:
 *
 * @code
 * examples/<module>/<example>/
 * |-- CMakeLists.txt       # native target definition
 * |-- <example>.ino        # Arduino entry point
 * |-- Shared.h             # portable entry point
 * |-- Shared.cpp           # code shown by the tutorial
 * `-- Desktop/main.cpp     # desktop adapter, when required
 * @endcode
 *
 * @section DspCore_Examples_Contents Tutorial index
 *
 * | Tutorial | What it explores |
 * | --- | --- |
 * | @ref DspCore_Example_CoreVersion | DspCore and Foundation version metadata |
 * | @ref DspCore_Example_LUTLine | One-dimensional storage, reserve and growth |
 * | @ref DspCore_Example_LUTSurface | Row-major two-dimensional storage and reshape |
 * | @ref DspCore_Example_LUTVolume | Three-dimensional storage, moves and overflow safety |
 * | @ref DspCore_Example_InterpolationLinear | Physical coordinates and linear extrapolation |
 * | @ref DspCore_Example_LUTSampling | Closed and periodic sampling in 1D, 2D and 3D |
 * | @ref DspCore_Example_GeneratorsPeriodic | Oscillator phase conventions |
 * | @ref DspCore_Example_GeneratorsShaping | Normalized nonlinear shaping |
 * | @ref DspCore_Example_GeneratorsEnvelopes | Stable exponential and logarithmic curves |
 * | @ref DspCore_Example_GeneratorsLUTEnvelope | Envelope mapping from a lookup table |
 * | @ref DspCore_Example_GeneratorsNoise | Reproducible stateful noise blocks |
 * | @ref DspCore_Example_GeneratorsWindows | Symmetric analysis windows |
 * | @ref DspCore_Example_FiltersFIR | 10- and 100-tap moving-average filters |
 * | @ref DspCore_Example_FiltersBiquad | Low-pass/high-pass Biquad crossover |
 * | @ref DspCore_Example_FiltersIIR | Generic normalized IIR recurrence |
 * | @ref DspCore_Example_AnalysisLevels | Peak and RMS measurement |
 * | @ref DspCore_Example_AnalysisEnvelope | Attack/release envelope following |
 *
 * @section DspCore_Examples_DesktopTools Desktop output and plotting tools
 *
 * `examples/Tools/` contains optional host-side helpers for the filter
 * tutorials. These scripts are not part of DspCore, are not compiled into an
 * Arduino sketch, and are not needed by an embedded consumer.
 *
 * | File | Purpose |
 * | --- | --- |
 * | `plot_signal.py` | Reads a signal CSV and produces a PNG with NumPy and Matplotlib. |
 * | `plot_signal.m` | MATLAB equivalent of the Python plotter. |
 * | `render_signal.sh` | macOS/Linux wrapper for the Python plotter. |
 * | `render_signal.ps1` | Windows PowerShell wrapper for the Python plotter. |
 *
 * `examples/Tools/` has no `CMakeLists.txt` because these are scripts rather
 * than build targets. The examples build copies them beside its executables;
 * exported Release examples ship them beside the launcher. Doxygen uses only
 * the versioned PNG snapshots in `Images/`, so reading the documentation never
 * requires Python or MATLAB.
 *
 * The filter adapters write CSV files to `~/Documents/DspCoreExampleOutput/`
 * by default. Select another directory with `--output` and render a result:
 *
 * @code{.bash}
 * ./build/macos_arm64/bin/Debug/DspCore_Filters_FIR_d --output ./output
 * ./build/macos_arm64/bin/Debug/render_signal.sh ./output/fir_moving_average.csv
 * @endcode
 *
 * @code{.matlab}
 * plot_signal("output/fir_moving_average.csv")
 * @endcode
 */

